 Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
 
+## Logout
+
+A volunteer can end a member's session right away with `logout(member_id)` in `larder/sessions.py`, for cases such as
+a stolen phone that was left logged in. A cookie is self-verifying rather than looked up, so logout does not delete a
+row; it records the moment and `verify` rejects any cookie issued before it, by comparing the logout time to the
+cookie's expiry minus `EXPIRY_MINUTES`. A member can log back in immediately after.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Logout is held in the web server's memory, not in Postgres, so it only stops cookies verified by the server that
+  received the call. [Sessions were moved out of server memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+  because that split sessions across servers behind the load balancer; the same split applies to logout until it is
+  backed by the same Postgres table. Workaround: also change the member's password, which invalidates login on every
+  server.
+
